d, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `src/money.py`'s docstring says it uses banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually used ROUND_HALF_UP. Because of that, `round_money(2.665)` returned 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use ROUND_HALF_EVEN. It was a one-line change plus the import, committed as 08d3cd5986.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory tool doesn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring.\n\nThe PR is not merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}